11
00:53:25,714 --> 00:53:31,714
Searching is a 2018 American screenlife mystery thriller film directed by Aneesh Chaganty in his
feature debut, written by Chaganty and Sev Ohanian and produced by Timur Bekmambetov.

12
00:58:17,142 --> 00:58:23,142
Set almost entirely on computer screens and smartphones, the film follows a father (John Cho) trying to find his
missing 16-year-old daughter (Michelle La) with the help of a police detective (Debra Messing).

13
01:03:08,571 --> 01:03:14,571
This was the first mainstream Hollywood thriller
headlined by an Asian-American actor.

14
01:08:00,000 --> 01:08:06,000
A co-production between the United States and Russia, the film
premiered at the Sundance Film Festival on January 21, 2018.

15
01:12:51,428 --> 01:12:57,428
It was released in a limited release on August 24, 2018, before
opening wide on August 31, 2018 by Sony Pictures Releasing.

16
01:17:42,857 --> 01:17:48,857
The film was a financial and critical success, grossing over $75 million worldwide against a $880,000 budget and
receiving praise for its direction, acting, unique visual presentation, and unpredictable storyline.

17
01:22:34,285 --> 01:22:40,285
At the Independent Spirit Awards, Cho was nominated for Best Male Lead.

18
01:27:25,714 --> 01:27:31,714
The film's success launched a titular film series including a standalone
installment titled Run, and a follow-up titled Missing.

19
01:32:17,142 --> 01:32:23,142
The film explores themes of california, stalker,
disappearance, internet, east asian lead.

20
01:37:08,571 --> 01:37:14,571
The tone is intense and emotional and mind_bending.
